From 6b65a17f5b1a28fe1494c2bc7954e9fa15c7d417 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeromy <jeromytann@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:40:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Use the society's wording for the /start welcome

Replaces the welcome copy with ZH's version and registers the command
names it advertises, so none of them answers with silence:

  /subscribeqn  -> same handler as /weeklyquiz
  /unsub_qns    -> same handler as /stopweekly
  /unsub_notes  -> same handler as /stopmonthly
  /practice was already an alias of /quizme.

The welcome no longer lists /review, /stats or /resources; /help still
does. The "->" arrows are escaped as -&gt; because the message is sent as
HTML.

test_welcome_only_names_commands_that_exist still requires every command
in the welcome to be registered, but no longer requires it to be in the
menu, since the society's names are aliases. A new test checks each alias
reaches the same handler as the command it stands for.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nuc625m5Lx4uuL3GmgUgMZ
